cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Rootless Computing Manifesto"
message: "If you cite or build on this work, please use the metadata below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Bădiță"
    given-names: "Florin"
    alias: "Vivi"
    website: "https://badita.org"
    orcid: ""
abstract: >
  Rootless Computing names a category of software with no origin server: the
  repository is the distribution, the browser is the runtime, the user's machine
  is the database, peers coordinate directly, and trust (when needed) is proved
  cryptographically rather than asserted by a host. The manifesto codifies the
  principles, vocabulary, and prior art.
keywords:
  - rootless computing
  - rootless apps
  - local-first
  - peer-to-peer
  - static sites
  - bake-time backend
  - mesh apps
  - zero-knowledge proofs
